    "problem_statement": "# Fillup option not working correctly for TextFSM parser\n\nI've found an issue with the `Fillup` option in TextFSM. When using this option, it's not correctly filling values in previous records as expected.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nHere's a simple example that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nimport textfsm\n\ntemplate = \"\"\"Value A (.*)\nValue Fillup B (.*)\n\nStart\n  ^${A}$$ -> Record\n  ^${B}$$ -> Record\n\"\"\"\n\ninput_text = \"\"\"value1\nvalue2\nvalue3\nfillup_value\n\"\"\"\n\nparser = textfsm.TextFSM(template_file=io.StringIO(template))\nresults = parser.ParseText(input_text)\n\nprint(results)\n# Expected: [['value1', 'fillup_value'], ['value2', 'fillup_value'], ['value3', 'fillup_value']]\n# Actual: [['value1', None], ['value2', None], ['value3', None], [None, 'fillup_value']]\n```\n\nThe `Fillup` option is supposed to fill in values for all previous records that don't have this value set. In this case, when we encounter the `fillup_value`, it should be applied to all previous records in column B.\n\nInstead, it seems the logic is reversed - it's stopping when it finds a record with the column already filled, rather than stopping when it finds a record with the column empty. Also, it's setting values to `None` instead of using the actual value.\n\nThis is breaking my parsing of network device outputs where some values appear later in the output but should be applied to earlier records."
